# Maximum Number of Items From Sale I

**Problem:** [LeetCode - Maximum Number of Items From Sale I](https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-number-of-items-from-sale-i/)

## Approach: Recursion + Memoization (DP)

- Use recursion to explore the possible choices for each item.
- At every index, consider three possibilities:
  1. **Take the current item once:** Add its contribution along with the remaining recursive result.
  2. **Take the current item again:** Reduce the budget and stay at the same index.
  3. **Skip the current item:** Move to the next index without changing the budget.
- Use an `unordered_map` to precompute the number of other items whose values are divisible by the current item's value.
- Apply memoization using `dp[index][budget]` to avoid recalculating states.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int dp[1001][1501];
    unordered_map<int,int> mp;

    int solve(vector<vector<int>>& items, int budget, int index) {
        if(index >= items.size()) return 0;

        if(dp[index][budget] != -1)
            return dp[index][budget];

        int max_count = 0;
        int pivot = items[index][1];

        if(pivot <= budget) {
            int c2 = 1 + mp[items[index][0]] +
                     solve(items, budget - pivot, index + 1);

            int c1 = 1 +
                     solve(items, budget - pivot, index);

            max_count = max(max_count, max(c1, c2));
        }

        int c3 = solve(items, budget, index + 1);

        return dp[index][budget] = max(max_count, c3);
    }

    int maximumSaleItems(vector<vector<int>>& items, int budget) {
        memset(dp, -1, sizeof(dp));

        int n = items.size();

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int pivot = items[i][0];

            if(mp.count(pivot)) continue;

            mp[pivot] = 0;

            for(int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if(i == j) continue;

                int num = items[j][0];

                if(num % pivot == 0)
                    mp[pivot]++;
            }
        }

        return solve(items, budget, 0);
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

Let:
- \(N\) = Number of items
- \(B\) = Given budget

| Operation | Complexity |
|---|---|
| Precomputing divisibility counts | \(O(N^2)\) |
| DP states | \(O(N \times B)\) |
| Each DP state | \(O(1)\) |

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(N^2 + N \times B)\)
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(N \times B + N)\), including DP and recursion stack (excluding the input array).
